   "prompt_sha256": "e20829bd7058d1fa6a138d36b3ef0b3a607224e87fe89f01608e1932c035df20",
   "prompt": "You are a careful literature curator coding an optogenetic screen for a blinded study of *Drosophila* descending neurons\n(DNs). You have no access to any model, simulation or prediction, and you must not look for one.\n\nYour room contains `PROTOCOL.md` (read it completely first and follow it exactly; section 8 is new), `record_schema.json`,\n`atlas_line_ids.csv`, `assigned_sources.csv`, `sources/` (the Cande et al. 2018 atlas with its figures and source data,\nalready downloaded) and `out/`.\n\nSession: `atlas-codeB`. Pass: `pass1`. Record IDs: `atlas-codeB-0001`, ...\n\nTask: for EVERY driver line the atlas tested (those in `atlas_line_ids.csv` and any other you find in its figures and source\ndata), write one record to `out/records.jsonl` for each preparation in which the atlas tested that line (a headless test\nand an intact test of the same line are two records; PROTOCOL section 1), coding the effect of activating it, by line ID, from the paper's\nfigures, figure legends and source data: put the line ID in `driver_lines` and `name_in_paper`, write `manc_type` as\n`UNMAPPED`, `mapping_confidence` as `low` and `mapping_basis` as `atlas line; type assigned later by script`\n(PROTOCOL section 8). Code every label field from what the atlas reports for that line (PROTOCOL sections 2-4), with a\nverbatim quote of at most 25 words or, where the evidence is a figure or table cell, a quote of its label and an exact\nlocator (figure, panel, table row). You do not know, and must not try to find out, which DN types the lines label.\nFinish with `out/dispositions.csv` (PROTOCOL section 8) and `out/notes.md`.\n\nRules: never use a model or simulation result; never visit the sites listed in PROTOCOL section 6; write only inside `out/`.\nSave records as you go.\n"
  },
  {
   "tag": "phaseb",
   "pid": 58316,
   "start_utc": "2026-11-21T00:29:59Z",
   "resumed_session": "b28784d7-1091-4aa9-8892-b30a8ea5102e",
   "prompt_sha256": "eeaa2d9ddde4997e11cb3f2cbc438931068b791a7b7dddf34829a83aa81b102f",
   "prompt": "Phase B (quote verification). Your Phase A records are saved; do not change `out/records.jsonl` or `out/not_found.csv`\nfrom now on.\n\nA new file is now in your room: `quotes_to_verify.csv` with columns `exp_id, doi, source_locator, quote` (quotes written by\nthe first reader). For each row, check in the local copy of the source (`sources/`) whether the quote occurs at or near the\nlocator (allow differences in whitespace, punctuation, line breaks and ligatures; do not allow different words). Write\n`out/quote_checks.csv`, a CSV file whose first line is the header `exp_id,quote_found,where,comment`, where `quote_found` is\nexactly `true` or `false` and `where` names the place you found it (or where you looked). Same rules as before: no model or\nsimulation results, no banned sites, write only inside `out/`.\n",
   "files_added": {
    "quotes_to_verify.csv": "4327dea31736e292ebfdfd24decdf2785239ad052b0d40fc1f161e3d513a83a1"
